{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Supergood Solutions public API",
    "version": "1.1.0",
    "summary": "Public reads of the rate card and service list, the fit-check POST with Idempotency-Key, and a sandbox that sends nothing.",
    "description": "The fit check is POST https://supergood-intake.vercel.app/api/intake. Two GET documents, /pricing.json and /services.json, are static files on https://supergood.solutions. No API key, bearer token, or account is required. See https://supergood.solutions/auth.md.\n\nIdempotency. POST /api/intake accepts an Idempotency-Key header (1 to 200 printable characters, no spaces). A retry with the same key and the same body within 24 hours does not send a second email. The same key with a different body is 422 idempotency_conflict. Without the header, each POST sends one email.\n\nSandbox. POST /api/sandbox/intake takes the same body, runs the same validation and sends nothing.\n\nRate limits. Every intake response carries RateLimit-Limit, RateLimit-Remaining, RateLimit-Reset and RateLimit-Policy. A 429 adds Retry-After. /api/intake allows 10 requests per 10 minutes per IP and /api/sandbox/intake allows 30. The limit is kept in memory per server instance, so treat it as approximate.\n\nVersioning. The API is version 1 and every intake response carries API-Version: 1. This document is 1.1.0. 1.1.0 added the Idempotency-Key header, the sandbox, the RateLimit headers and the JSON 404, and removed nothing. A breaking change ships as a new path, for example /api/v2/intake. The old path keeps working for at least 90 days after the change is announced on https://supergood.solutions/developers/ and in this description, and during those 90 days it returns Deprecation and Sunset headers. Adding a response field or an optional request field is not a breaking change. pricing.json and services.json are unpaged and cannot send Sunset or Deprecation headers (GitHub Pages), so a change to them is announced on the developers page.\n\nThe same fit check is the submit_fit_check tool on the MCP server at https://supergood-intake.vercel.app/api/mcp (card: https://supergood.solutions/.well-known/mcp/server-card.json).",
    "contact": {
      "name": "Ryan Sandoval",
      "url": "https://supergood.solutions/start/",
      "email": "ryan@supergood.solutions"
    }
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://supergood-intake.vercel.app",
      "description": "Intake API host. Fit check, sandbox, and the JSON index at GET /."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://supergood.solutions",
      "description": "Static JSON documents served by GitHub Pages."
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "reads",
      "description": "Side-effect free JSON documents."
    },
    {
      "name": "intake",
      "description": "Fit-check submission. Each accepted POST emails Ryan."
    },
    {
      "name": "sandbox",
      "description": "Same validation as the fit check. Sends nothing."
    }
  ],
